{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/841104-2e-your-house-rules","id":841104,"title":"2e: Your House Rules?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-02T21:06:06-08:00","id":841104,"title":"2e: Your House Rules?","content":"I'm really curious to see what kind of house rules people use for Second Edition now that people have had a few years to roll around in it for a while. I'll start with mine.<br /> <br /> 1) You always have a Touchstone, unless you or someone else, or nature, kills it. The Touchstone merit exists solely to let you have more than the one single Touchstone you always have. Incidentally, this means the Ventrue clan bane becomes 'Ventrue have to put more effort to get something out of having a Touchstone, because that first default one doesn't give them any bonus dice - it just counts for keeping them from having the -2 penalty for having no Touchstone at all.'<br /> <br /> 2) You start with a bonus dot in both of your clan's Favored Attributes, rather than having to choose just one.<br /> <br /> The reason behind these is pretty simple in my mind. For the first, I find it a little silly that you have to pay what is essentially an XP tax to keep engaging with the Touchstone mechanics after you pass a certain Humanity threshold. In my experience it just becomes irrelevant after a point. This way the whole thing stays in play longer.<br /> <br /> For the second, I just like to have starting characters get a little more kick to them, and to make them a bit better out of the gate at doing the things their clan does even if they weren't the best candidate for it before they died.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T21:14:22-08:00","id":841108,"title":"","content":"I've always used one rule from Mirrors: rather than assign Primary/Secondary/Tertiary for your Attributes and Skills, you instead total it all up and spend it from a pool. So instead of 5/4/3 and 11/7/4, it's just 12 and 22 assigned however you want with nothing going over 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T21:16:54-08:00","id":841109,"title":"","content":"I let the Predatory Aura Conditions be applied more than once a month.<br /> <br /> It makes things more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T23:35:21-08:00","id":841161,"title":"","content":"Matched combat defense. Base Defense+Brawl if your in a brawl, Base Defense+Weaponry if you're up against someone fighting you with a knife, etc, with Athletics used only for full dodge and ranged attack defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T02:20:40-08:00","id":841180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/841104-2e-your-house-rules?p=841109#post841109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I let the Predatory Aura Conditions be applied more than once a month.<br /> It makes things more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Particularly considering Uratha impose similar conditions without such restriction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T04:59:33-08:00","id":841226,"title":"","content":"Nothing too big, I allow conversions of Vampire the Masquerade disciplines and certain, few, disciplines from first edition Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T05:48:30-08:00","id":841243,"title":"","content":"Pretty much just an update of 1e material to 2e: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1KzmfRtypNdYDofYUTl4IzMJEB1sPqdNF1eWiX9fJSLI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> I did do some hacks concerning Revenants (specifically to associate them with Belial's Brood and the Therion bloodline from 1e, oh and a name change to &quot;Ghast&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T06:18:39-08:00","id":841256,"title":"","content":"I remember nerfing the Swarm Form, making it so the Gangrel's attack pool was two times her Protean score. That always felt too powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T06:24:27-08:00","id":841263,"title":"","content":"signature has a link to mine","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T10:35:29-08:00","id":841379,"title":"","content":"I have a few custom bloodlines rolling in my game with homebrew disciplines. I have also made a Blood Sorcery character that didnt do cruac or theban, but it was more of an odd mix of both,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T10:49:31-08:00","id":841387,"title":"","content":"First and foremost, I make vampires straight up immune to bashing damage unless the attack would normally inflict &quot;roll-over&quot; damage into lethal in its single attack. It just doesn't make sense to me that a vampire can treat a bullet to the head as being as serious as a punch in the jaw, and then actually feel a punch in the jaw.<br /> <br /> I make it possible for vampires to learn all disciplines, even those that would normally be bloodline-exclusive, without actually joining a bloodline. However, learning a bloodline-exclusive discipline without belonging to that bloodline requires a much higher XP - I normally require dots * 1 for &quot;clan/bloodline favored&quot; disciplines, dots * 2 for general disciplines, and dots * 3 for restricted disciplines. Additionally, you need to come up with a believable reason why/how your vampire can learn to force their Blood to bestow these powers, and you're likely to face in-universe problems if you're treading on a monopoly or attitudes about the sacredness of such powers.<br /> <br /> I also make it possible for any vampire to join any bloodline, but it's much easier for &quot;founding&quot; clanmembers to do so. It would take a very special kind of Daeva to want to join the Macellarius, even if she would have relatively few problems impressing them enough to accept her.<br /> <br /> I convert a lot of disciplines from Masquerade into Requiem as well, often making them bloodline, clan or covenant &quot;restricted&quot; - that is, they're held by a specific group, so it's very difficult to learn them without getting &quot;in&quot; on that group.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the Macellarius, I don't use them. I use Nelapsi and let them have Gustus as their bloodline discipline instead. They're also able to learn Phagia, just like the Noktuku.<br /> <br /> These are the ones I can think off of the top of my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T17:56:57-08:00","id":841619,"title":"","content":"A simple one I like and have used: the Gangrel clan attribute increase is Stamina or Resolve (instead of Composure). Not that your average Nomad isn't capable of having social graces or coolness under fire, but given their Curse, they feel less Composed than, well, Resolute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 03-20-2016, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T03:46:26-08:00","id":842938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/841104-2e-your-house-rules?p=841387#post841387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I make it possible for vampires to learn all disciplines, even those that would normally be bloodline-exclusive, without actually joining a bloodline. However, learning a bloodline-exclusive discipline without belonging to that bloodline requires a much higher XP - I normally require dots * 1 for &quot;clan/bloodline favored&quot; disciplines, dots * 2 for general disciplines, and dots * 3 for restricted disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is for 2E? Scaling XP costs have been eliminated entirely, why are you bringing them back for Discipline house rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T16:25:34-08:00","id":843178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/841104-2e-your-house-rules?p=841387#post841387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First and foremost, I make vampires straight up immune to bashing damage unless the attack would normally inflict &quot;roll-over&quot; damage into lethal in its single attack. It just doesn't make sense to me that a vampire can treat a bullet to the head as being as serious as a punch in the jaw, and then actually feel a punch in the jaw.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your ideas intrigue me and I wish to subscribe to your newsletter.<br /> <br /> How has this worked in game?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T17:55:49-08:00","id":843221,"title":"","content":"@Inodiv: I had forgotten about that little change in 2e. The list I gave was off the top of my head, so I may have some of the mechanics wrong.<br /> <br /> @Tabanese: Can't really say, unfortunately. I've never actually run a game. No group to play with. Besides which, I'm not really much of a storyteller, alas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T06:33:00-08:00","id":843387,"title":"","content":"I use three hacks from Armory reloaded I highly recommend <br /> <br /> Vampires take bashing from anything that isn't a bane, sunlight or fire. Even head shots (there are vampires in books with no brains. They're not loving in any sense of the word so why do guns hurt?)<br /> <br /> Also healing while feeding, feeding heals 1 lethal or two bashing per vitae consumed as if they spent it to heal reflexively at the moment of feeding. They may still spend the vitae consumed to heal if needed obviously.<br /> <br /> Vampires can drain vitae equal to stamina in one turn rather then just 1, this makes stamina important again and makes Ganges very, very scary. My player has stamina at four and resilience at 3 he can drain 7 vitae with a single bite and combined with healing hack above? Makes Vampires very scary and balances with other templates well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T06:39:42-08:00","id":843391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/841104-2e-your-house-rules?p=843387#post843387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I use three hacks from Armory reloaded I highly recommend<br /> <br /> Vampires take bashing from anything that isn't a bane, sunlight or fire. Even head shots (there are vampires in books with no brains. They're not loving in any sense of the word so why do guns hurt?)<br /> <br /> Also healing while feeding, feeding heals 1 lethal or two bashing per vitae consumed as if they spent it to heal reflexively at the moment of feeding. They may still spend the vitae consumed to heal if needed obviously.<br /> <br /> Vampires can drain vitae equal to stamina in one turn rather then just 1, this makes stamina important again and makes Ganges very, very scary. My player has stamina at four and resilience at 3 he can drain 7 vitae with a single bite and combined with healing hack above? Makes Vampires very scary and balances with other templates well.</div> </div> </div> </div>And BP 2 Vampires can basically drain a person in 2 turns if you let them take +4 to their stamina with Physical Intensity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T06:44:03-08:00","id":843394,"title":"","content":"Physical intensity adds dice to a pool, not dots to an attribute. It's a subtle difference, but here and there it matters.<br /> <br /> Also in 2E a vampire drains whatever successes they roll, capped by blood potency. So at BP 7 + they are quite capable of draining an average mortal dry in one go, even by RAW. Admittedly making this stamina instead does give them even more of an edge in that regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-07-2016, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T07:20:22-08:00","id":843414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https: